cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, cite this software and the relevant original mathematical sources."
title: "HeavyTailedNoise: Lean 4 formalization of stochastic optimization bounds"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Xiong"
    given-names: "Zhixiao"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xiong-zx/heavy-tailed-noise-lean"
version: "0.2.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of the complete finite-q lower bound for arbitrary
  randomized strict-K=1 algorithms and the original strict-K=1 shared-batch
  exponential-memory upper algorithm in the same gradient-only model.
  Under the common absolute accuracy condition, a verified corollary gives
  matching rates for the same dimension-uniform minimax complexity. The
  library also verifies the separate first-slot-normalized Fradin v2
  Theorem 3.1 in its zero-respecting shared-seed batch model. The local
  421-module canonical build, independent public-entry import, and 30-entry
  public signature and axiom audit passed on 30 September 2026. The
  package does not claim an infinite-q theorem.
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "stochastic optimization"
  - "heavy-tailed noise"
  - "complexity lower bounds"
  - "complexity upper bounds"
  - "formal verification"
